    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0564" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.93/6–2551: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-06-25T15:00:00+03:00">June 25, 1951—3 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Unnumbered. Strictly eyes only for the Secretary personally. This is Embassy’s
                    third this special series. Embassy Secretary again called at Peiping Embassy 12
                    noon today 25th with view either (1) <pb facs="0565" n="549" xml:id="pg549"/>
                    delivery informal note or (2) inquiry whether Peiping Ambassador would meet me
                    privately. Chinese doorman after apparently seeking instructions in Embassy
                    stated no one available to receive Secretary and no use his waiting.</p>
                <p>In circumstances I conclude that Peiping Ambassador, who must have been informed
                    calls last Friday<anchor n="1" xml:id="d357-f1"/> and today, not prepared have
                    direct contact us here. There is, of course, channel of approach thru Russians
                    and Swedes. If you desire utilize either of those, I suggest the Swedes but note
                    Ambassador Sohlman<anchor n="2" xml:id="d357-f2"/> plans leave Moscow vacation
                    Wednesday June 27. Doubt advisability using Indians and Indian Ambassador in
                    Paris in any case.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d357-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d357-f1" n="1" xml:id="d357-f1-content">
                <p>June 22; see the unnumbered telegram on <ref target="#pg545">p. 545</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d357-f2" n="2" xml:id="d357-f2-content">
                <p>Rolf Sohlman, Swedish Ambassador in Moscow.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d357-f3" n="3" xml:id="d357-f3-content">
                <p>No further messages in this series have been found in the Department of State
                    files, nor any evidence that there were additional messages.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
